# 0001. Record architecture decisions as .adr files

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

## Context
The config's decisions lived in commit messages, README "review" sections and code comments.
A future reader (or Claude) had to dig through history to learn why things are the way they are.

## Decision
Record decisions with long-term consequences as ADRs in `docs/adr/NNNN-short-title.adr`:
sequential four-digit numbers, never reused, markdown content, the `.adr` extension so they are
told apart from other docs. `docs/adr/README.md` is the index. Earlier decisions (0002–0012) are
recorded retroactively from the repo's history.

## Alternatives
- Keep decisions in README sections: mixed with usage docs, no status or supersession.
- `.md` extension: works everywhere, but ADRs can't be told apart from other markdown.

## Rationale
One place, one format, with a status that shows whether a decision still holds.

## Consequences
- Commits carry `[ADR-NNNN]` tags (`commit-style`).
- `.adr` needs editor support: see [0012](0012-adr-files-in-the-editor.adr).

## References
- `adr-manager` skill
